{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-14T12:35:43.107Z","author":"codex-rl-apvf-1114","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0ef7f263adcb9d8f457f1402","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-14T12:35:43.107Z","author":"codex-rl-apvf-1114","text":"Final targeted evidence for the configured-terminal collection slice (main base b2c1cfbd950d674183d5713b2f90d165efcb5f7b):\n\nFresh packed public CLI run: unbraind/pm-ops at eba7d5262fd75e67afce0caad29dae7dc7dfbaeb; copied source and controller are non-git scratch projects. All 300 durable source files remain unchanged (SDK runtime caches excluded). Corpus snapshot e45e6205eddf35edc2167d253a2ef1fb5ce2a4c4116557497f1e24da2230b656; programme digest 17720f2c1e58043c8374024cfe63b25c710b0d11ada35705690dd4b0e6dd58c2. There are 105 training and 41 held-out items. Existing examples/loop-corpus.json thresholds and schedule are unchanged; a separate scratch Decision approves two promotions, 16 optimizer updates, 10000 wall milliseconds, 524288 staging bytes, 2000 CPU milliseconds and zero tokens.\n\n| Generation | Source checkpoint SHA-256 | Candidate checkpoint SHA-256 | Exact held-out | Sampled incumbent -> candidate | Decision |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | 17493680209cdf2fc86126ff2ad0b7bb6063ae24ce00f28f931224bb5ab2fd11 | 2df645949b852625c2acdc20bf5232620cac8c87d1ab1f8f85c4221da14ac605 | 0.5979768545815656 | 0.499825 -> 0.597650 | promote |\n| 2 | 2df645949b852625c2acdc20bf5232620cac8c87d1ab1f8f85c4221da14ac605 | 3e31b06286e99d6b3d73486216f98f0c6d519228cac4bcbefc56f4945c292863 | 0.6810112913266447 | 0.595100 -> 0.685825 | promote |\n\nGeneration two collected with generation one's promoted checkpoint. Real rl loop resume returns the same terminal checkpoint; independent post-replay SDK reads confirm exactly two jobs and unchanged checkpoint bytes and resource charges. Both jobs settle eight updates once; 512 collection samples total and 40000 evaluation episodes per side per generation. This is finite-corpus adaptive validation, not independent tracker transfer power. Complete minimized implementation/artifact hashes, sealed decisions, process charges and replay receipts are in docs/history-status-roles-evidence.json; explanation and the fresh gap table are in docs/recursive-improver.md.\n\nBehavioral reverts, each in a disposable copy with retained tests: (1) projectImproverHistory literal terminals; (2) trackerHistoryExample literal statuses; (3) buildImproverDataset omits registry forwarding; (4) committedTrackerStatusRegistry reads working settings. All four npm run typecheck commands exit 0 and all four selected regression commands exit 1 on assertions. Commands are node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"SDK roles\" test/history-status-roles.test.ts for (1)/(2), and the same command with --test-name-pattern=\"improver builder pins\" for (3)/(4). Restored complete regression file passes 3/3.\n\nFinal targeted coverage run passes 18/18; the additional existing source-path test passes 1/1. Touched files: 462/462 lines, 305/305 branches, 79/79 functions; the repo's V8 statement measurement over these fresh exact-source reports is 303/303 blocks. All four thresholds remain 100. Linked pinned pm test run passes 3/3. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run lint, npm run docstring (572 declarations) and npm run duplicates (zero clones) pass. Full release certification is delegated to exact-head CI as requested. No new SDK gap or dependency-pin change. Follow-up pm-rl-prefix-status-roles tracks the separate history-prefix vocabulary; this item stays in progress for orchestrator verification.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-14T12:35:43.1